<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Varanasi</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Benares, Banaras, Kashi</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Varanasi, also called Benares or Kashi, is a city on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ganges-plain">Ganges</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uttar-pradesh">Uttar Pradesh</a>, northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, and one of the holiest cities of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hinduism">Hinduism</a>. Pilgrims bathe and cremate the dead at its riverside ghats, and the Kashi Vishwanath temple is dedicated to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shiva">Shiva</a>. The Buddha preached his first sermon at nearby <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sarnath">Sarnath</a>. In the 18th century it became the seat of the Rajas of Benares.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/varanasi.jpg" alt="Varanasi" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Vyacheslav Argenberg · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Varanasi,_India,_Ghats,_Cremation_ceremony_in_progress.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
